Hash: SHA512

annotations:
  artifacthub.io/changes: |
    - kind: changed
      description: "The azure, digitalocean, linode and custom presets no longer set ingressClassName: nginx, since ingress-nginx was retired upstream. Their Ingress has no class, so the cluster's default IngressClass serves it; set ingress.className to pick a controller. The aws (alb) and gke (gce) presets are unchanged."
    - kind: added
      description: "Optional Gateway API HTTPRoute (httpRoute.enabled, httpRoute.parentRefs, httpRoute.hostnames) attaches the edge to a Gateway you already run. clientIP.mode auto then trusts the one X-Forwarded-For entry the Gateway appends, and the install notes show the route and warn when the edge Service is also a LoadBalancer."
    - kind: added
      description: "New HTTP/3 guidance (CUSTOMIZATIONS.md, How do I serve HTTP/3?): HTTP/3 belongs between clients and your TLS terminator, and a CDN or L7 load balancer is the recommended place for it, because UDP load balancers can't send PROXY headers and fair-share admission would lose the client IP. A per-provider table records what each load balancer supports; Linode NodeBalancers can't carry HTTP/3 today."
    - kind: fixed
      description: "Corrected the Linode guide: LKE is x86-64 only; HA control planes and Premium NodeBalancers don't need LKE Enterprise; the CCM has no label annotation and ignores loadBalancerSourceRanges (use firewall-acl); leave the NodeBalancer throttle off; Block Storage volumes go up to 16 TB. It now covers firewalling LKE nodes, so clients can't reach the NodePorts directly and forge a PROXY header, pinning the NodeBalancer IP with preserve and nodebalancer-id, NodeBalancer connection limits, and egress IPs that change with the autoscaler."
  artifacthub.io/signKey: |
    fingerprint: C3A55111ED91FEDE4A82A4B4463266060957C4B3
